docs {
  # GET /courses/{id}
  
  Retrieves course additional metadata (price type, duration, level, benefits, video, etc.).
  
  ## HTTP Method & Route
  - **Method:** `GET`
  - **Route:** `/wp-json/tutor/v1/courses/:id`
  
  ## Authentication
  - **With API key + JWT:** user must be able to view the course.
  - **Without API key:** public courses always; non-public courses only if `student_must_login_to_view_course` is off.
  - Guests do **not** receive `course_settings`.
  
  ## Path Parameters
  
  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `id` | `integer` | **Yes** | Course post ID. |
  
  ## Responses
  
  ### 200 OK (Success)
  
  Meta fields use `get_post_meta( ..., false )`, so most values are **arrays** (often a single-element array).
  
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_course",
    "message": "Course detail retrieved successfully",
    "data": {
      "course_settings": [
        {
          "maximum_students": 100,
          "content_drip_enabled": 0
        }
      ],
      "course_price_type": ["paid"],
      "course_duration": [
        {
          "hours": "4",
          "minutes": "30"
        }
      ],
      "course_level": ["all_levels"],
      "course_benefits": ["Learn modern web development principles."],
      "course_requirements": ["Basic knowledge of HTML and CSS."],
      "course_target_audience": ["Beginner developers."],
      "course_material_includes": ["Source code, Certificate."],
      "video": [
        {
          "source": "youtube",
          "source_youtube": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=example",
          "source_vimeo": "",
          "source_external_url": "",
          "source_embedded": "",
          "source_shortcode": "",
          "source_video_id": "",
          "poster": ""
        }
      ],
      "disable_qa": false
    }
  }
  ```
  
  `video` is the stored `_video` meta shape (`source` + `source_youtube`, …), not the Pro write body `{ source_type, source }`.
  
  ### 404 Not Found
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_course",
    "message": "Detail not found for given ID",
    "data": []
  }
  ```
}
